    "source": "Bad Eden Bulwark + Shadow Courier v1.0 (RFI-native rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Every threshold you have ever crossed remembers you. You may now ask one to remember you out loud.</em></p><p><strong>Unfound Route — 1/session.</strong> As an action, name two thresholds you have personally crossed earlier in this campaign (any door, arch, gate, ward, or hex boundary your character has crossed at least once before). You travel from one to the other directly, by way of the spaces in between that don't exist on any map.</p><ul><li><p>You may bring up to <strong>4 willing allies</strong> with you.</p></li><li><p>The journey takes <strong>one hour of subjective time</strong> regardless of actual distance, terrain, hostility, or planar boundary. You arrive somewhat changed by the experience.</p></li><li><p>The destination threshold must still exist (not destroyed, sealed against you specifically, or relocated).</p></li><li><p>You cannot use Unfound Route to enter a place you have not been, to escape an active combat round, or to cross a threshold someone else used (only your own).</p></li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
